## PRIMARY VISION

I do not want a conventional planetary information website where a user clicks Earth, Moon or Mars and reads basic facts.

I want an immersive, browser-based 3D space exploration game in which a student genuinely feels like an astronaut exploring another world.

The target experience should have the visual and interaction quality of a professionally developed third-person exploration game, using the polish, camera presentation, character scale, movement responsiveness, environmental detail and immersive world design associated with high-quality games such as BGMI as a QUALITY REFERENCE ONLY.

Do not copy BGMI's copyrighted characters, maps, weapons, interface, sound effects or gameplay mechanics. Cosmic Explorer remains a peaceful educational scientific exploration game, not a shooter or combat game.

The user should be able to enter the universe, travel to Earth, land on the Moon or Mars, walk freely through actual 3D environments, observe realistic landscapes, inspect scientific objects, listen to educational narration, collect discoveries and complete scientific exploration missions.

The most important success criterion is that the game must FEEL PLAYABLE AND IMMERSIVE, not merely look like a beautiful 3D illustration.

